      "Threshold 0.90: spread changed by -99.33% and mean adopter rating proxy changed by -0.0284 relative to the no-threshold baseline.",
      "The largest measured spread reduction among thresholds with a non-negative proxy change was at threshold 0.80: -99.09% versus baseline, with an adopter-rating-proxy change of 0.0265. This is the measured spread/satisfaction trade-off; the proxy is simulator-side, not an observed satisfaction rating.",
      "A threshold can reduce low-affinity adoption, but the measured table, not an assumed monotone effect, is the evidence. The rating proxy is simulator-side and is not observed satisfaction."
    ],
    "limitations": [
      "The adopter rating proxy (1 + 4 * affinity) is predicted by the recommender, not observed after the intervention.",
      "The intervention is applied inside the simulator; no online randomized experiment was run.",
      "Shared simulation seeds reduce but do not eliminate path-level randomness when a threshold changes the cascade."
    ]
